# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Take Me Home — local Docker certification environment.
#
# You do not fill this in by hand. `npm run docker:start` writes .env.docker
# from the running stack's own status, so the file always describes the stack
# you actually have rather than the one the template was written against.
#
# This copy exists to document the contract and to be explicit about what the
# values are.
#
# WHAT THESE VALUES ARE
# ---------------------
# The Supabase CLI's local development credentials. Every checkout of every
# project on every machine produces the same ones — they are published in
# Supabase's own documentation. They authorise nothing beyond the containers on
# this machine, and `npm run docker:reset` destroys the database they belong to.
#
# They are not production credentials and must never be treated as a stand-in
# for them. Nothing here is, or may become, a copy of:
#
#   SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN     the hosted management token
#   SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD      the hosted database password
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY the hosted key that bypasses row-level security
#
# Those live in GitHub Actions secrets and reach the hosted workflow only.
# scripts/docker/lib.sh removes them from the environment of every local
# command, so a shell that has them exported still cannot point a local reset
# at the hosted project.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The stack's API gateway, as seen from the host.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321

# Public by contract — protected by row-level security, not by secrecy.
# Both generations are written by the start script; the app prefers the first.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_local_development_key
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...local-development-anon-jwt

# Bypasses row-level security. Server-side only, run time only, and local only.
# It is never a Docker build argument: build arguments survive in image history.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_local_development_key

# The stack's PostgreSQL, for the schema and policy suites. Each suite builds
# its own throwaway database on this cluster.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres

# Where the browser suite points. Left unset, Playwright starts its own server.
E2E_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Iteration 6 / 14 — the AI provider.
#
# Runtime-only, and absent by default. When no provider is configured the
# planner reports unavailable; it does not return a stub plan, and no mock
# stands in for the provider. Setting a real key here lets a developer exercise
# the planner locally — it does not certify Iteration 6, which stays
# ENGINE_PARTIAL until a real provider request succeeds in a run that is
# recorded as evidence.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
